<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lothair III, Holy Roman Emperor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1075">1075</a>–<a href="/years/1137">1137</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Lothair of Supplinburg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lothair-i">Lothair</a> III, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a>, was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duke-of-saxony">Duke of Saxony</a> from 1106, King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> from 1125 and emperor from 1133. As duke he granted Holstein and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stormarn">Stormarn</a> to Adolf I of Schauenburg in 1111 and encouraged expansion against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a> east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a>. His alliance with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-welf">Welfs</a> shaped German politics after his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lothair-iii-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="Lothair III, Holy Roman Emperor" width="267" height="384" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lothair_II,_Holy_Roman_Emperor.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Lothair of Supplinburg</b> then became duke and, in 1125, king; his heir was his son-in-law Henry the Proud of the Welf family.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-saxony">Duchy of Saxony · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>The new kingdom had to be defended by force: Pope Innocent II, Emperor <b>Lothair III</b> and rebellious mainland barons and cities fought Roger for most of the 1130s.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-sicily">Kingdom of Sicily · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1134 Emperor <b>Lothair III</b> gave the Northern March to Albert the Bear of the House of Ascania.</blockquote><a href="/empire/margraviate-of-brandenburg">Margraviate of Brandenburg · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1111 <b>Duke Lothair of Saxony</b> granted the County of Holstein and Stormarn to Adolf I of Schauenburg.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-holstein">County of Holstein</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1111 <b>Duke Lothair of Saxony</b> granted Adolf I of Schauenburg the County of Holstein, beginning a long double rule over Holstein and the Weser lands.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-schaumburg">County of Schaumburg</a></li></ul></section>
